// ── GERMAN GRAMMAR SHEETS ─────────────────────
// One sheet = one bite: the structure as coloured blocks, one line on
// why it works that way, up to four numbered rules, a table or a list,
// examples, the trap — and a small quiz (3 questions drawn from the
// sheet's 3–5, so a retake asks others). The verb track (verb-track.js) brings each sheet into Today
// the first time its tense is taught; all of them are also in
// ☰ › 📐 Grammar.
//
// Markup in the strings: **bold** · [[verb]] = the verb, in the tense's
// colour · `term` = a block-coloured term.
//
//   struct  [[text, kind]…] — kind: who · aux · verb · end · pre · p2 ·
//           inf · modal · refl · mid · thing
//   table   { head: [...], rows: [[...]] }  ·  lines: [[label, text]…]
//   mine    which of your verbs to list under it (verb-track.js)
//   quiz    { k: "type" | "pick" | "odd" | "order" | "why", q, a, o?,
//           why, chk? } — chk [inf, form kind, person]: the engine must
//           give the same answer (tests/verb-track.test.mjs checks it)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

